# Both images build from the REPO ROOT as context (the console's settings evaluation needs
# the root scripts and the version catalog, and the core's needs the console's build script),
# so one ignore file serves both. Each Dockerfile then COPYs only the paths it wants — layer
# caching keys on those, not on context size, so what is listed here is purely about what
# gets uploaded to the daemon on every build.
.git/
.gradle/
# Every build directory, at any depth: console/build holds the boot jar and the JaCoCo and
# Playwright reports, which dwarf the sources. A bare `build/` would only match the root one.
**/build/
# docs/media carries a local Playwright install once the README screenshots are regenerated
# (docs/media/README.md).
docs/
